    <string name="home_key_disclosure_title">Let the Home button open Matinee?</string>
    <string name="home_key_disclosure_body">Some TVs keep the Home button for their built‑in launcher and bring its home screen back after a restart. To open Matinee instead, Matinee uses an Android accessibility permission.\n\nIt sees only the remote\'s Home button and when the TV\'s built‑in home screen opens. It does not read what is on the screen, what you type, other keys or other apps, and nothing is sent anywhere.\n\nOn the next screen, choose “Matinee Home button” and turn it on. You can turn it off there at any time.</string>
    <string name="home_key_disclosure_accept">Agree and continue</string>
    <string name="home_key_restricted_title">Install Matinee from Google Play first</string>
    <string name="home_key_restricted_body">This TV doesn\'t let apps installed from an APK file use accessibility permissions, so the switch turns itself back off.\n\nUninstall Matinee, install it from Google Play, then turn this on again.</string>
    <string name="home_key_restricted_try">Try anyway</string>

